Falsifies `virtio::verification::a_configuration_read_holds_inside_one_generation`.

The defect: the generation is read again after the value but never compared, so the first read is
returned whatever the device did between the two generation reads. A resize between the two halves
of the capacity would pair one capacity's low half with another's high half.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(generations[0], generations[1])`, on a run whose two
generation reads differ.

diff --git a/crates/virtio/src/lib.rs b/crates/virtio/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/virtio/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/virtio/src/lib.rs
@@ -1335,3 +1335,3 @@ fn consistent_read(
         let value = read();
-        (generation() == before).then_some(value)
+        { let _ = (generation(), before); Some(value) }
     })
